/*
:name: attr_enable_no_value
:type: error
:error: needs a value
:help: enable=<condition>
*/
// The pin-attribute family (`enable`, `clock_pin`, `reset_pin`) NAMES A SIGNAL,
// so a flag-only spelling says nothing. The attribute grammar defaults a
// value-less attribute to the text `true`, so `:[enable]` used to sail through
// the frontend and surface much later as tolg's
//   reg 'r' names enable 'true' but 'top' has no such input/wire
// — a message about a signal the user never wrote. Reject it at the source,
// where the span still points at the attribute.
//
// The old flag-only `clock`/`reset` attributes are gone (since ruling 52 a
// clock or reset is declared by its type, `:Clock`/`:Reset`);
// attribute_clk_renamed.prp and attribute_reset_vs_reset_pin.prp cover those
// spellings.
pub mod ennoval(clk:Clock, rst:Reset, d:U8) -> (q:U8@[]) {
  reg r:U8:[clock_pin=clk, reset_pin=rst, enable] = 0 // locate_error_here
  r = d
  q = r
}
